\f1\b0 \
We are creating a website with an online interactive map of colleges in Florence, Italy and the  surrounding area. It\'92s got basically all of the colleges that are that are based in Florence, including all of the away foreign campuses such as NYU, and it\'92s got information on each college in each program, number of students, demographic info about them, and links to their website and other resources as available. If you click on an entry that\'92s the interactive part, it shows you details. In addition to a layer with college info, it has two other layers.  One is a layer with great study spots in Florence where you can park it with a laptop and sip a cappuccino, and no one will bother you if you hang out.  Another is a layer with great bars/eateries/nightlife spots for college students on a budget.  \
\
For each layer, do research on the web to read reviews and synthesize a recommendation score (from online reviews, Reddit, other sources). In the additional info include the rec score and quotes and links.  Do a comprehensive search and include only the top places, maybe top 15% of all the places available, maybe about 50 places max for each layer. Use your judgment on this. It should be a curated list.\
\
The home page is the map, with a prominent way to include all three layers.  There is also an interactive chat.  There is a chat for each school and for like a big chat for all the schools but in order to access the chat, you need to have a verified domain or like a recognized domain so you need to have a school email address from one of the colleges that is listed and recognized. So you have to have a registration page and people have to register a verified email address to access the chats. The site would send them a verification link when they register so you know it\'92s a real email, and there would be an access control list.\
\
The style should be modern and sophisticated. Search for a modern theme compatible with a cool college site.  Build and deploy on Github Pages at https://github.com/torwager/collegeinflorence.\
